# Phase 3 remoting transport review — 2026-09-27

- Baseline: Java RocketMQ 5.5.1 remoting client sources in `/Users/nanashi07/Projects/3rd/rocketmq`; Rust inventory `docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md`.
- Reviewed processor dispatch and executor lifecycle: Java inbound work is submitted to processor-specific/default executor (default `publicExecutor`), and rejected work returns SYSTEM_BUSY; Rust resolves the same selection and maps executor rejection/panic to SYSTEM_BUSY. Rust's default public executor and inbound queues are unbounded; Java default public executor is `Executors.newFixedThreadPool` and also uses an unbounded queue. Tokio staging queues, task scheduling/thread identity and lifecycle remain different and are not waived for observable queue/error behavior.
- Reviewed callback path: Java callback executor is caller-provided or the fixed public executor, falls back inline on submission failure, and public callback order is complete then succeed/fail after channel establishment; initial connect failure reports fail only. Rust mirrors executor routing, inline fallback, order, and initial-failure handling with read-only result context; callback worker/thread lifecycle and Rust-native error types remain differences.
- Reviewed event path: Java event executor is a `ServiceThread` polling its queue at up to 3-second intervals; queue admission is at most 10001. Rust uses a capacity-10001 Tokio MPSC queue and a start-owned worker. Address-only listener callbacks and Tokio polling/shutdown lifecycle are explicitly accepted; this does not waive admission or event/control-flow parity.
- Verified Java config/lifecycle details: fixed `publicExecutor` is constructed in client constructor; processor/event workers start during `start`; shutdown closes channels and calls shutdown on event, Netty, public and scan executors without awaiting complete drain. Rust explicitly starts and joins owned work with its shared bounded shutdown policy; accepted Tokio lifecycle/thread differences remain recorded.
- Reviewed phase verification boxes against tests and latest local validation. Marked P3-V01, P3-V02, P3-V03, and P3-U01 checked in both English and Traditional Chinese plans as local test evidence only. P3-V04 remains unchecked and deferred to Phase 19. No Phase 3 completion or Phase 4 start is declared.
- Validation passed after the latest code change: `cargo fmt --all --check`, `cargo test --workspace --offline` (49 remoting unit, 4 codec integration, 74 transport integration plus workspace tests), `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --offline -- -D warnings`, `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`, `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`, and `git diff --check`.
- Commits created: `a1c0056 fix(remoting): bound scans and retain transport error context`; `8e2bbb2 docs(remoting): record phase 3 parity review evidence`. Remaining plan/rlog changes require review and commit. Phase 3 remains unaccepted; remaining `PARTIAL` executor/lifecycle and Java/Rust observable parity dispositions must be resolved before acceptance. Phase 4 must not start.
